  "response_text": "Procrastination is a common problem that can lead to missed deadlines and poor performance on exams. Here are some warning signs to watch for with severe procrastination and missed deadlines with an emergency exam-week plan:\n\n1. You consistently start your work late and finish it early.\n\n2. You frequently skip important deadlines and fail to meet your goals.\n\n3. You procrastinate on important tasks and assignments.\n\n4. You avoid difficult tasks and assignments.\n\n5. You frequently miss deadlines and fail to meet your goals.\n\n6. You procrastinate on important tasks and assignments.\n\n7. You avoid difficult tasks and assignments.\n\n8. You frequently miss deadlines and fail to meet your goals.\n\n9. You procrastinate on important tasks and assignments.\n\n10. You avoid difficult tasks and assignments.\n\nIf you are experiencing any of these warning signs, it is important to take action to address the issue. You may need to set more realistic goals, prioritize your tasks, and create a schedule to help you stay on track. It may also be helpful to seek support from a friend, family member, or a professional to help you manage your time and stay on track.",
